"""
NLSY79 extract (data/nls_raw.csv): How is the advantage in BA degree completion for Black
students related to SES level?

Pre-registered design (approved by researcher):
 OUTCOMES  P3 PRIMARY : highest grade completed 1979 >= 12, among respondents aged >=20 in 1979
           P1 SECOND  : grade >= 13 (full sample, grade observed)
           P2 SECOND  : ever residence == 3 (DORM/FRAT/SORORITY) 1981-1996, among those with
                        at least one observed residence year
           APPENDIX   : grade >= 16 ("BA-or-higher grade"), descriptive only, exact CIs
 SES      PRIMARY  : background-only index (1979): z(max(par grade)) + z(-occ code) + z(log inc),
                     >= 2 of 3 items, pooled-sample cuts; granularity rule: tertiles only if every
                     race x level cell n>=100 for primary outcome, else 2 levels (pooled median)
           SENS     : occupation dropped / continuous, complete-case, missing-indicator,
                     endogenous 1985/1990/1996 wealth & income & savings
 CONTROLS  age 1979 linear+quadratic, sex; ASVAB mean Z added in one "does gap attenuate" spec
 MODELS    logistic, BLACK x SES interaction + LR test. No imputation of the outcome.
"""
